Restrict scan length in email name and http auth (CVE-2026-59887)

The `src_auth` and `src_email_name` regex fragments used unbounded `+`/`*`
quantifiers. On pathological inputs (e.g. `mailto:mailto:mailto:...`), the
`:` in the schema prefix is also a valid email-name char, so each of the
O(n) schema hits re-scans to the end of the tail, giving O(n^2) work and a
ReDoS-style hang. Cap the scanned lengths (auth <= 50 chars, email name <=
64 chars per RFC 5321) so scanning can no longer run to the end of the input.

Backported from upstream commit 105e5d77f7d119871d2b2d86ed208568eb3e7ffe,
remapping lib/re.mjs (ESM) onto lib/re.js (CommonJS). The published npm
tarball for linkify-it@2.2.0 ships only lib/re.js (no test/ directory), so
the upstream test/pathological.mjs regression test is omitted here; the
runtime fix in lib/re.js is the security-relevant change.

